  "audio": "016.that-is-why.mp3",
  "paragraph": 16,
  "text": "That is why tiny harness bugs can silently wreck your cloud bill. Put a live timestamp with seconds inside your system prompt, and you bust the entire prefix cache on every single turn. Dynamically reordering tool schemas between turns does the exact same damage. Mutating an earlier message in the middle of the loop invalidates every token downstream of that edit. Great harnesses keep the prefix immutable, and only append new messages to the end of the conversation.",
